{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "2026-10-25T04:44:26.765595+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-25T04:44:27.481004+00:00", "id": 23633300, "conceptrecid": "23627826", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23633300", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23627826", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23633300", "metadata": {"title": "Packing unit squares in a square of side just below an integer: a two-strip construction with O(\u221aK) deficit", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23633300", "publication_date": "2026-10-25", "description": "<p>Let s(n) be the side of the smallest square containing n non-overlapping unit squares. We show that for every integer K &ge; 16, s(n) &lt; K whenever n &le; K&sup2; &minus; 8&radic;K &minus; 19; equivalently, the wasted area is W(s) &le; 8&radic;K + 19 for s in [K &minus; 1/K, K). The best known general bound W(s) = O(s^{3/5}) gives only a deficit of order K^{3/5} in this regime. The proof is an explicit construction: two strips of squares tilted by an angle of order K^{&minus;1/2}, one on the bottom wall and one on the right wall, with an axis-parallel grid elsewhere. Version 2 adds a proposition: thicker strips, giving g &ge; 2 extra squares per column, beat the grid for every fixed g once L is large, but with wasted area of order L^{2/3}, so the single-gain strips are the best choice. Exact rational certificates of 2824 improved upper bounds (1184 &le; n &le; 9944) are deposited at https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23624432.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Karimi, Mohsen", "affiliation": "Independent researcher, Zanjan, Iran", "orcid": "0009-0004-1055-8267"}], "keywords": ["square packing", "wasted area", "upper bounds", "discrete geometry"], "version": "V2.0", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "alternate_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.23624433"}], "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": 